number|title|condition|evidence|remediation|limitation|attack|nist|nist_rationale|sources|severity
001|Privileged group membership exceeds the approved roster|An effective member of a defined control-plane group is outside the approved dated administrator roster.|Group SID; transitive membership with scope; account state; approved roster and exceptions.|Remove unnecessary privileged membership after owner review.|Without an approved roster, report ReviewRequired rather than declaring every unfamiliar member unauthorized.|T1078.002|AC-2;AC-6|Review and limit standing privileged account membership.||High
002|Protected-object ACL control is delegated outside the intended tier|An unapproved principal has an effective owner or DACL-control path to a protected privileged AD object.|Object classification; security descriptor; inheritance; effective-access derivation; approved tier.|Restrict ownership and DACL changes to the protected administrative boundary.|AdminCount alone does not establish current privilege; evaluate actual protection and account use.|T1098|AC-3;AC-6;CM-5|Protect authorization data for privileged accounts.||High
003|AdminSDHolder has an unintended effective editor|An unapproved principal can make a security-relevant change to AdminSDHolder or its security descriptor.|Exact object DN/SID context; owner/DACL; effective access; supported propagation semantics.|Remove the unintended edit path and review protected-object permissions.|Do not assume any directory read or attribute permission grants DACL control.|T1098|AC-3;AC-6;CM-5|Protect the template used to maintain permissions on protected accounts.||High
004|Computer-account creation exceeds the approved delegation|Effective machine-account creation authority or quota permits principals beyond the approved provisioning scope.|ms-DS-MachineAccountQuota; OU-specific creation delegation; account type; approved join workflow.|Restrict computer provisioning to approved identities and locations.|A positive quota is not an RBCD exploit. Authorized join workflows and OU delegation must be considered separately.|T1136.002|AC-2;AC-6;IA-4|Limit who may create domain identities and where they are provisioned.||Medium
005|Unconstrained delegation exists outside the approved service set|A non-DC computer or service identity has effective unconstrained delegation without an approved documented requirement.|Delegation flags; object type; service ownership; approved exceptions.|Remove unnecessary delegation and review the service's authentication design.|DCs have different requirements; do not apply a blanket non-DC recommendation to them.|T1558|AC-6;IA-5|Limit delegation and exposure of authentication material.||High
006|Anonymous directory access exceeds the approved scope|Effective directory configuration permits anonymous access to nonpublic information outside the approved requirement.|Directory access settings; applicable ACLs; anonymous scope; approved publication requirement.|Restrict anonymous access to explicitly approved information.|Do not equate ordinary authenticated directory reads with anonymous access.|T1087.002|IA-2;AC-3|Require appropriate authentication and authorization for directory information.||Medium
007|DNS update permissions exceed the approved record-owner scope|An unapproved principal can modify security-relevant AD-integrated DNS records or zone configuration.|Zone update mode; record/zone ACL; ownership; effective access; approved DNS delegation.|Restrict DNS updates and remove stale or overly broad record ownership.|Secure dynamic updates do not make every record ACL safe; conversely authenticated registration alone is not malicious.|T1557|AC-3;CM-5;SC-20|Protect authoritative name resolution data and its modification rights.||Medium
008|Replication rights are granted outside the approved service inventory|A principal has the complete effective permission set for sensitive domain replication and no approved service or DC role justifies it.|Domain-root ACL; required extended rights; nested groups; service inventory; approved exceptions.|Remove unjustified replication authorization after dependency review.|A single replication-related ACE does not prove secret replication capability.|T1003.006|AC-6;IA-5|Limit access to directory replication of sensitive authentication information.||High
